add('expansion-v3-finite-loop-gain','Finite-gain amplifier compares VIN with output feedback beta times VOUT. Open-loop gain is 1000 and feedback fraction is 0.1.','This is a feedback signal-flow diagram of the stated linear model.',box(310,90,190,90,['A = 1000'])+path('M500 135H625M625 135V265H290M160 135H310')+`<circle cx="135" cy="135" r="25" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/>`+path('M65 135H110M135 160V265H165')+box(165,232,125,66,['β = 0.1'])+text(91,113,'+')+text(113,184,'−')+text(65,110,'VIN')+text(635,114,'VOUT')+arrow(480,265,365,265)+note('No input current, output resistance or load.'));
add('expansion-v3-buck-ripple','Ideal buck power stage: 12 volt input connects through a controlled high switch to switching node SW, with a complementary ideal low switch from SW to ground. A 60 microhenry inductor feeds 3 volt output, capacitor and 6 ohm load.','Ideal complementary switches represent the lossless buck switching states.',box(92,64,148,52,['High switch'])+path('M45 90H92M240 90H320')+text(65,52,'12 V')+dot(285,90)+path('M285 90V177')+box(225,177,120,60,['Low switch'])+path('M285 237V305H640')+inductor(320,90,535,90,'60 μH')+path('M535 90H640')+capacitor(535,90,535,305,'C large',-1)+resistor(640,90,640,305,'6 Ω')+ground(430,305)+text(585,55,'VOUT = 3 V')+note('100 kHz; continuous conduction; high switch on for D · T.',356));
add('expansion-v3-boost-duty','Ideal boost topology: 5 volt input through an inductor to a switch node. An ideal switch connects that node to ground. A forward diode connects switch node to the output capacitor at 12.5 volts.','The switch conducts for fraction D of each period.',text(60,79,'5 V')+inductor(75,115,285,115,'L')+path('M285 115H420M285 115V200')+dot(285,115)+box(225,200,120,60,['Switch'])+path('M285 260V310H605')+path('M420 95L455 115L420 135ZM455 93V137M455 115H605')+capacitor(605,115,605,310,'C')+ground(445,310)+text(580,85,'VOUT = 12.5 V')+note('Ideal diode; CCM steady state; output voltage constant per cycle.',355));
add('expansion-v3-linear-regulator-loss','A linear regulator takes 5 volts and supplies 3.3 volts at 300 milliamperes. Input and output current are equal.','Quiescent current and other power paths are neglected.',flow(['5 V','IIN = IOUT'],['Linear regulator'],['3.3 V','IOUT = 300 mA'],'Find the power dissipated inside the regulator.'));
add('expansion-v3-adc-step-code','Ideal 12-bit unipolar ADC takes 1.65 volts, uses 3.3 volt reference and outputs a code from zero through 4095.','The exact floor rule is specified in the problem.',flow(['VIN = 1.65 V','VREF = 3.3 V'],['Ideal 12-bit ADC','4096 quantization bins'],['Code = ?'],'Find the LSB voltage and output code.'));
add('expansion-v3-adc-quantization-noise','Quantization-error probability density is uniform between minus q over two and plus q over two, where q is 1 millivolt.','The rectangle shows a probability density, not a time waveform.',path('M105 260H640M360 290V65',muted)+path('M140 260H205V130H515V260H590',accent)+text(195,286,'−q/2')+text(525,286,'+q/2')+text(625,286,'Error')+text(385,76,'Probability density','start')+note('q = 1 mV; zero-mean uniform error model.'));
add('expansion-v3-debug-divider-open','Nominal divider: 5 volts across two 10 kiloohm resistors. Ideal meter reads node A at 5 volts. Supply and upper resistor are verified; one listed fault is present.','Nominal topology shown. The fault is intentionally not drawn.',divider({v:'5 V',r1:'10 kΩ',r2:'10 kΩ',foot:'Measured VA = 5 V; ideal meter draws no current.'}));
add('expansion-v3-debug-feedback-open','Nominal inverting amplifier uses 0.10 volt input, 10 kiloohm input resistance and 100 kiloohm feedback. Plus input grounded. Measured output is minus 4.5 volts and minus input is about 0.10 volts.','Nominal topology shown. Use both measured voltages to infer the fault.',inverting({vin:'+0.10 V',rf:'100 kΩ',foot:'Measured: VOUT = −4.5 V and V− ≈ +0.10 V.'}));
add('expansion-v3-debug-probe-loading','A step source drives output through 100 kiloohms. Node has 10 picofarads to ground, and the connected probe adds 90 picofarads in parallel.','The probe has infinite resistance but nonzero capacitance.',source(120,185,'Step')+path('M120 130V72M120 240V280H565')+resistor(120,72,355,72,'100 kΩ')+path('M355 72H565')+capacitor(355,72,355,280,'10 pF',-1)+capacitor(565,72,565,280,'90 pF')+ground(430,280)+text(560,44,'Probe')+note('Time constant: 1 μs without probe; 10 μs with probe.'));
add('expansion-v3-debug-adc-reference','A 12-bit ADC sees unknown actual input and reference voltages; intended input is 1.024 volts and assumed reference is 2.048 volts. Observed code is 1024.','The observed code alone does not identify which voltage is wrong.',flow(['Actual VIN = ?','Actual VREF = ?'],['12-bit ADC','Code readout verified'],['Observed code: 1024'],'Intended VIN = 1.024 V; assumed VREF = 2.048 V.'));
add('expansion-v3-buffered-filter-cascade','Two 1 kiloohm and 100 nanofarad low-pass stages are isolated by an ideal unity-gain buffer. Final output is unloaded.','The buffer prevents the second RC stage from loading the first.',resistor(45,110,215,110,'1 kΩ')+capacitor(215,110,215,290,'100 nF',-1)+ground(215,290)+path('M215 110H295')+box(295,70,130,80,['Ideal buffer','Gain = 1'])+resistor(425,110,590,110,'1 kΩ')+capacitor(590,110,590,290,'100 nF')+ground(590,290)+text(50,85,'vIN')+text(620,86,'vOUT')+note('Evaluate the cascade at the common RC corner frequency.'));

